WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
Drop a piece of potassium
into cold water,

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.070
and it fizzes and races
across the surface.

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.330
Drop in magnesium, and
almost nothing happens,

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.450
until you add acid.

5
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.550
Drop in gold, and nothing
happens at all, even in acid.

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.910
Now dip a more reactive metal
into a solution of a less

7
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.830
reactive metal's salt.

8
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.850
The less reactive metal is pushed
out, and coats the surface.

9
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.470
What single property ranks them all?

10
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.250
In this mission, you'll compare
how metals react with water and

11
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.870
with dilute acid, and build the
reactivity series from what you

12
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.420
see.

13
00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:38.490
You'll predict displacement reactions.

14
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.430
Your mission: find the one
property that puts every metal in

15
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.380
order.
